            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025:F026\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"49 CFR 392.10(a) establishes a mandatory stopping duty before crossing railroad tracks at grade, explicitly conditioned by '[e]xcept as provided in paragraph (b) of this section.' Paragraph (b)(1) specifies that a stop need not be made at a streetcar crossing or industrial switching tracks within a business district. Setting relation to 'exception' and qualifying C0000 accurately converts this prose caveat into an explicit qualification edge targeting the stopping duty baseline while preserving the correct 'not_required' modality.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F027\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) establishes the stopping requirement before crossing railroad tracks subject to the exceptions in paragraph (b). Paragraph (b)(2) explicitly exempts drivers from stopping at a grade crossing when directed to proceed by a police officer or crossing flagman. Updating C0010 to have an 'exception' relation qualifying baseline claim C0000 faithfully reflects this statutory exception and preserves the appropriate 'not_required' modality.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F028\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) imposes the railroad crossing stop requirement except as provided in paragraph (b). Paragraph (b)(3) exempts crossings controlled by a functioning highway traffic signal showing a green indication permitting crossing without stopping or slowing under local law. Linking C0011 to baseline C0000 as an 'exception' accurately models this qualification edge while maintaining the proper 'not_required' modal force.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F029\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) establishes the baseline railroad crossing stop duty subject to paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(4) specifies that a stop need not be made at an abandoned railroad grade crossing marked with an abandoned rail line sign. Changing C0012's relation to 'exception' qualifying C0000 correctly establishes the structural link to the duty it qualifies while retaining the 'not_required' modality.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0004\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F025\", \"F030\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a) mandates stopping at grade crossings except as provided in paragraph (b), and paragraph (b)(5) explicitly provides that a stop need not be made at an industrial or spur line grade crossing marked with an 'Exempt' sign. Structuring C0013 as an 'exception' qualifying C0000 accurately captures the relationship to the stopping baseline and preserves the 'not_required' modality.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
